  "notes": "Market (5×6, D-054), three levels on a shared paved square. Level 1: the KayKit market hall with blue awnings at the back; in front a KayKit well, two awning stalls, crates, barrels and sacks, a bench by the road. Level 2: as level 1 plus an open roofed hall on six timber posts under terracotta with three goods tables in front on the right and two more awning stalls. Level 3: the KayKit hall gives way to a stone market hall (an arcade of stone piers, a plastered upper floor with windows, a hipped terracotta roof and a flag) with coloured awnings over goods tables in front of the arches; the roofed hall, stalls and well of level 2 stay.",
